+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two versions of a JSON document. The library can apply a JSON Patch but cannot produce one, so clients resend whole documents.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `createPatch(from, to)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returning a JSON Patch (RFC 6902) that `applyPatch` turns from `from` into `to`.
+- The patch is small: unchanged parts are not mentioned, nested changes are addressed by their own path, and array item insertions/removals are single `add`/`remove` operations that do not rewrite neighbouring items.
+- Inputs are never mutated; the patch shares no structure with them.
+- Governing standards: RFC 6902 (§4 operations, §4.6 equality, §3 patch shape) and RFC 6901 (§3, §5 pointer escaping). No breaking change: purely additive. Out of scope: `copy`/`test` operations, move detection beyond remove+add, minimal-byte guarantees, non-JSON inputs (`undefined`, functions, cycles).
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-patch-diff`: generating a JSON Patch from two JSON documents.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+`src/index.ts` (new export), new tests in `test/`, README section. No dependencies.
